  "source": "claude_session",
  "raw_text": "The claude_terminal launch script was updated to produce a .md twin of each session at close time. The pipeline on session exit became: script exits \u2192 gzip \u2192 col -b \u2192 .md saved to ~/logs/claude/ \u2192 session_extract.py reads from .md. This split was described as occurring at the capture layer rather than the inference layer. The .gz remains the crash-resilient bit-faithful archive; the .md is the first time the session exists as a human- and LLM-readable document. The .md is not a convenience \u2014 without it, any tool reading the raw .gz output would be replaying the terminal state machine, producing cursor jumps, screen clears, and overwritten text rather than prose.",
